            ],
            "note": "Source states this pair saves O and is used when the S/Z queue setups cannot be built; it gives no queue condition and no rule for choosing left or right. build_condition is derived, not quoted: placing the solve without HOLD requires I rests on J, Z on T, and L passes through row y=1, which only the image 8 T and J complete. tools/ijlo_solves.py verify plays all 5040 orders of the following bag (HOLD empty or occupied at the PC start) with SRS 90-degree movement and checks that the solve is reachable exactly when these prerequisites can be met with one HOLD slot (1344 orders). The two last_among terms are the S and Z queue fail conditions: the source uses this pair only when those setups cannot be built, so save O waits until both have failed. When both sides qualify, source order picks the left one (verified 2026-10-18)."
          }
